"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
3018,"Narrated to us Al-Rabee’ ibn Sulaymaan and Baḥr ibn Naṣr—both said: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who said: My father Abū al-Zinād informed me, on the authority of ‘Alqamah, from his mother, from ‘Ā’ishah (RA), who said:
“I used to love to enter the House (the Ka‘bah) and pray inside it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took me by the hand and brought me into the Ḥijr. He then said:
‘O ‘Ā’ishah! When your people rebuilt the Ka‘bah, they fell short and left the Ḥijr outside the House. So if you wish to pray inside the House, pray in the Ḥijr, for indeed it is a part of the House.’”

**CHAPTER:**"
3019,"###
 Narrated to us Al-Rabi', who said: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: Bahrun Nasr told us at the end of his narration: Ibn Abi al-Zinad said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aisha (RA), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If not for the recentness of your people's disbelief, I would"
